---
title: Pinned booking lifecycle and external effect ordering
---
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Selecting
    Selecting --> Validating: submit booking form
    Validating --> Selecting: validation, verification, limit or host failure
    Validating --> Seats: matched seated slot after validation
    Validating --> Existing: pending or round-robin duplicate found
    Validating --> Persisting: valid new request
    Persisting --> Pending: effective confirmation required or positive price
    Persisting --> Accepted: free without confirmation, or owner reschedule
    Persisting --> RejectedRequest: transaction or unique conflict
    Pending --> PaymentRequired: positive price and unpaid original
    Pending --> ProviderCreate: authorized confirmation, free or paid
    Pending --> Accepted: host confirms with payment row while unpaid
    PaymentRequired --> PaidPending: supported receipt and confirmation still required
    PaymentRequired --> PaidAccepted: supported receipt and no confirmation required
    PaidPending --> ProviderCreate: authorized host confirms
    PaidAccepted --> ProviderCreate: previously unconfirmed receipt fulfills after payment commit
    ProviderCreate --> ConfirmationNotice: returns results, including all integrations failed
    ConfirmationNotice --> Accepted: guarded dispatch, suppression or caught mail failure, then confirmation DB write
    Accepted --> FreshProvider: default-accepted fresh creation
    FreshProvider --> FreshNotice: returns results, including all integrations failed
    FreshNotice --> Accepted: guarded confirmed dispatch or suppression after initial DB write
    Accepted --> ProviderAttempt: already-accepted payment receipt
    ProviderAttempt --> Accepted: external outcome recorded separately
    Pending --> Rejected: authorized rejection, optional refund before status write
    PaidPending --> Rejected: authorized rejection and refund policy
    Accepted --> CancelWebhook: valid cancellation
    Pending --> CancelWebhook: valid cancellation
    CancelWebhook --> Cancelled: webhook attempt then DB cancellation
    Cancelled --> Cleanup: provider, refund, references, jobs and mail
    Cleanup --> Cancelled: later failures may be logged and success returned
    Accepted --> Replacement: reschedule transaction cancels original and creates replacement
    Pending --> Replacement: valid reschedule
    Replacement --> ProviderAttempt: provider reschedule follows DB commit
    Cancelled --> CancelRejected: cancelling unchanged cancelled original returns 400

    state "Existing seated slot" as Seats {
        [*] --> SeatRequest
        SeatRequest --> SeatLocked: lock booking row in transaction
        SeatLocked --> SeatFull: fresh count reaches positive capacity
        SeatLocked --> SeatCommitted: nested attendee and seat commit
        SeatCommitted --> SeatEffects: provider attendee update, payment and notification path
        SeatEffects --> SeatCommitted: partial external failure follows caller policy
        SeatCommitted --> AttendeeRemoved: valid seat and multiple attendees
        SeatCommitted --> WholeBookingCancel: last attendee or authorized whole-event cancellation
        SeatCommitted --> SeatMovedOrMerged: owner or attendee reschedule branch
    }
